Gemini:
I. The Khevsurians were at the guest-house, beer was brewing in the vessel;
They sat upon the flat roof and feasted, drinking it from bowls;
Some played the panduri, singing loudly to its tune,
Laying heroic tales as a bridge to the listeners' souls;
With fervor, they sacredly recounted the names of heroes in verse;
The elders smoked their pipes, the smoke enveloping them like mist,
They interpreted their deeds and offered blessings to the heroes' spirits.
To instruct the youth, they recalled them with praise:
"It is up to you now, whoever among you shall prove to be a man!"

